# External integrations and extraction

- Define explicit typed ports for email, OAuth, vision, and other integrations. Register production adapters through Nest providers and replace them at the provider boundary in tests.
- Apply finite request and connection timeouts. Validate provider responses and translate transport failures into stable application errors.
- Do not mutate global `fetch` or replace methods on live singleton providers in new tests; inject fake adapters or transports before creating the application.
- Do not make paid API calls, send real email, or contact live OAuth providers during automated tests.
- Validate uploaded image size, decoded format, pixel count, and animation/frame limits before calling vision. Do not trust the filename or supplied MIME type.
- Treat images and model output as untrusted evidence. Validate extracted fields and distinguish ambiguous, missing, and zero scores.
- Extraction returns a suggestion only. Persist a result only through an authorized, validated save workflow with concurrency checks and explicit user confirmation where required.
- Keep manual score entry available when vision is unavailable. Test timeout, malformed output, provider errors, ambiguous identities, and non-persistence of suggestions.
- Do not log image bytes or include credentials in provider diagnostics. Record safe latency, failure, and usage metadata.
